  "comment": "The polyphony is real and it is per channel: each of the thirty-two signal inputs is added into its row's bus one channel at a time, using its own channel count, and the matching signal output is given the width of the widest input on that row. The switch, scene and expander jacks are all read as channel one only. Four of them — the two step jacks and the two that pair with them — count any voltage other than 0V as high, negative voltages included, so no threshold is written for those."
